[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:6. Percy Buttons]
[00:00.980] Passage 6 | 文章六
[00:02.590] Percy Buttons | 波西·巴顿斯
[00:05.455] I have just moved to a house in Bridge Street. | 我刚搬到⼤桥街的一所房子里。
[00:10.110] Yesterday a beggar knocked at my door. | 昨天一个乞丐敲了我的门。
[00:13.485] He asked me for a meal and a glass of beer. | 他向我要一顿饭和一杯啤酒。
[00:17.450] In return for this, | 作为回报，
[00:19.525] the beggar stood on his head and sang songs. | 乞丐倒立着唱歌。
[00:24.065] I gave him a meal. | 我给了他一顿饭。
[00:26.545] He ate the food and drank the beer. | 他吃了食物，喝了啤酒。
[00:30.010] Then he put a piece of cheese in his pocket and went away. | 然后他把一块奶酪放进口袋里就走了。
[00:34.565] Later a neighbor told me about him. | 后來一位邻居告诉了我关于他的事。
[00:38.175] Everybody knows him. | 人人都认识他。
[00:40.350] His name is Percy Buttons. | 他的名字叫波西·巴顿斯。
[00:43.235] He calls at every house in the street once a month | 他每月到街上每家每户拜访一次，
[00:47.290] and always asks for a meal and a glass of beer. | 并且总是请求一顿饭和一杯啤酒。